-- title:
--   Unramified additive characters of G_{ℚ_p} span at most a line
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $k$ a field. Write $G_p$ for `primeLocalGaloisGroup (pPrime p)`, the group of $\mathbb{Q}_p$-algebra automorphisms of the algebraic closure `PadicAlgCl p` of $\mathbb{Q}_p$, and let `primeLocalToGlobal` be the homomorphism $G_p \to \operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ obtained by restricting scalars to $\mathbb{Q}$ and then restricting an automorphism to the algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$ inside `PadicAlgCl p`. Consider the set of functions $\varphi : G_p \to k$ subject to three conditions: (i) $\varphi(\sigma\tau) = \varphi(\sigma) + \varphi(\tau)$ for all $\sigma,\tau$; (ii) $\varphi(\sigma) = 0$ whenever $\sigma$, viewed as an automorphism of `PadicAlgCl p`, lies in the inertia subgroup of the valuation subring [`padicIntegers p`](def/GaloisRep_CompletionBridge.html#L20) over $\mathbb{Q}_p$, i.e.\ in the image in $G_p$ of the inertia subgroup inside the decomposition subgroup; (iii) there exists an intermediate field $F$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$, finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}$, such that $\varphi(gs) = \varphi(g)$ for all $g,s \in G_p$ with the image of $s$ in $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ fixing $F$ pointwise. The assertion is that the $k$-submodule of $G_p \to k$ spanned by this set is finite-dimensional over $k$ and that its $k$-rank is at most $1$.
--
--   This is the bound $\dim_k H^1_{\mathrm{nr}}(\mathbb{Q}_p, k) \le 1$ for additive characters of the local Galois group that are trivial on inertia and of finite level, the unramified line being cyclic and generated by a Frobenius lift. It is used in the local count bounding unramified diagonal deformations, via [`ResidualGaloisRep.finiteDimensional_ordinaryUnitClassesAd_and_finrank_le`](thm.html#ResidualGaloisRep.finiteDimensional_ordinaryUnitClassesAd_and_finrank_le).
